From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom-qmp-combo: glymur: let the DP lane pair follow the orientation

On the Glymur USB43DP combo PHY the DP TX blocks are the USB3 lane blocks,
and the block USB3 occupies follows the physical cable orientation (block A
in normal, block B in reverse orientation, selected through
QPHY_V3_DP_COM_TYPEC_CTRL).  The DP PCS lane-pair selection was forced to
lanes 2/3 through dp_mode_ignore_reverse, so in reverse orientation DP
kept its PCS on the pair that carries the live USB3 link while the lane
table went into the other block: every reverse-orientation replug on a
Surface Laptop 8 failed link training at the first repeater with USB3
unaffected, and every normal-orientation replug worked.

Let the DP PCS lane pair follow the orientation like every other QMP combo
PHY: lanes 0/1 (block A, DP_PHY_MODE 0x4c) in reverse, lanes 2/3 (block B,
0x5c) in normal orientation.  This matches the reverse-dependent
driver-enable and bias selection qmp_v8_configure_dp_phy() already makes.

Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -3469,7 +3469,6 @@
 
 	.dp_aux_cfg2		= QSERDES_DP_PHY_AUX_CFG2_V8,
 	.dp_phy_cfg1		= QSERDES_DP_PHY_CFG1_V8,
-	.dp_mode_ignore_reverse	= true,
 	.dp_lanes_exclusive	= true,
 
 	.regs			= qmp_v8_n3_usb43dpphy_regs_layout,
@@ -3490,9 +3489,10 @@
  * only the block that carries its lanes while USB3 shares the port (USB3DP
  * mode, DP on two or one lanes).  The block USB3 occupies follows the cable
  * orientation (block A in normal, block B in reverse orientation), so DP
- * takes the other one: block B in normal, block A in reverse.  This is
- * independent of dp_mode_ignore_reverse, which only concerns the DP PCS's
- * own lane numbering.  In DP-only mode DP owns both blocks.
+ * takes the other one: block B in normal, block A in reverse.  The DP PCS
+ * lane-pair selection (qmp_combo_configure_dp_mode()) has to follow the
+ * orientation as well, so dp_mode_ignore_reverse must stay clear on such a
+ * PHY.  In DP-only mode DP owns both blocks.
  */
 static void qmp_combo_dp_lane_blocks(struct qmp_combo *qmp, bool *use_tx,
 				     bool *use_tx2)
